        "fontFamily": "sans-serif"
      },
      "data": {
        "label": "EXAMPLE — Modernization Drivers & Goals\n\nIllustrates: a motivation view (drivers → goals → objectives), labeled edges rather than a sequence or hierarchy of systems — deliberately markdown-heavy, this gallery's flagship use of the details sublayer. Every node has real, substantial detail behind it; the diagram itself is deliberately just the map.\n\nPersona: the modernization task force itself, working through why the program exists.\n\nColor key: red = drivers (external/internal pressures). Amber = goals (what the program aims to achieve). Green = objectives (measurable targets under each goal).\n\nPart of the Meridian Rail example gallery — epic 0022 (docs/planning/epics/0022-example-diagram-gallery.md)."
      }
    },
